            "review_title": "Review at Ốc Ngon Nha Trang",
            "review_text": "Food & Beer\nNha Trang, Vietnam11 contributions\n0\nReview of a Good Snail Restaurant in the Nha Trang City Center\nJun 2025 • Friends\nI had the chance to visit this snail restaurant on a weekend evening and would like to share some personal impressions.\n\nLocation and Ambience:\nThe restaurant is located in a central area, easy to find, with an open and airy space. The seating is simple, suitable for casual dining. However, it gets quite crowded during peak hours, so you may have to wait for a table if you arrive late.\n\nFood Quality:\nThe seafood here is generally fresh. The dishes are well-prepared, retaining the natural sweetness of the ingredients. I ordered several items including salted fried sweet snails), grilled blood cockles with scallion oil, steamed clams with lemongrass , and fried crab claws with tamarind sauce. The food was served fairly quickly, seasoning was flavorful, and the dipping sauce was balanced—not too salty or too sour.\n\nService:\nThe staff were attentive and quick, with no mistakes in taking the order. However, when the restaurant gets busy, food preparation time may be a bit longer. The service attitude was acceptable—not overly friendly but not unpleasant either.\n\nPricing:\nThe prices are reasonable for the food quality and location. Each dish ranges from 80,000 to 125,000 VND. A group of three people can enjoy a filling meal for around 500,000 VND.\n\nConclusion:\nThis place is a good choice for those looking to enjoy fresh snails and seafood at an affordable price in a casual and comfortable setting. Nothing too fancy, but the quality is reliable. I would return if I have the chance.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nGoing in a small group makes it easier to find a table and allows you to order a variety of dishes to share, which is both cost-effective an\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten June 18, 2025",
